error[ffi_union_field]: this construction of `UT` names `i` and `f`, which are the same bytes: `ffi-a-construction.h` declares `UT` a `union`, so C would keep only the one written last
  at tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs-2137-a-value-only-the-probe-sees-is-told-beside-a-union-built-from-two-members.hero:21:9
     |
  21 |     u = UT(i: 1, f: 1.5)  #~ ffi_union_field
     |         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  note: a `record` over a C union names one or more of each union's members and reads any, and is built naming exactly one, an anonymous struct's fields counting as one (§ 13): name the one the program writes

error[ffi_constant_type]: `K_DIV` in `fixedbugs-2128-values.h` cannot be declared `i64`: clang refuses the header's value at line 4: its expression holds an operation C leaves undefined for the operands it is given, and the program's own unit, built with clang's checks for an overflow, a shift, a division by zero and a float out of an integer's range, traps where it reads it
  at tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs-2137-a-value-only-the-probe-sees-is-told-beside-a-union-built-from-two-members.hero:18:5
     |
  18 |     constant K_DIV: i64  #~ ffi_constant_type
     |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  note: `fixedbugs-2128-values.h` line 4 reads `#define K_DIV ((-2147483647 - 1) / -1)`
  note: an operation C leaves undefined gives no value: wherever C computes it, a program reading `K_DIV` reads whatever the machine held. A group's `constant` is the value C computes from the header (§ 13): correct the value there, or bind a constant whose value C defines
